.TH RECOVER.SH 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.3.3" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
recover.sh \- unknown wallet file to sweep, with human confirmation at each step
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
recover.sh FILE DEST [\-\-chain C] [\-\-goal addresses|balance|sweep] [\-\-url ESPLORA|RPC] [\-\-fee\-rate N] [\-\-count N] [\-\-chain\-id N] [\-\-password\-file F]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
recover.sh: unknown wallet file \-> classify \-> right reader \-> funded addresses \-> sweep
transaction to DEST \-> human confirms signing \-> human confirms broadcast.
.PP
The front door for every recipe in recipes/README.md. \-\-goal addresses prints public addresses
only (DEST is ignored, pass \-), balance also asks the chain, sweep (default) builds, signs, sends.
\-\-chain picks the chain for seeds and raw keys (default btc). Sweep is automated for btc, ltc, doge
(UTXO) and eth; every other chain stops after the addresses (exit 3) and names its builder + recipe.
.IP \(bu 2
Secrets never touch the disk or this script's variables: keys() re\-runs the reader
pipeline each time it is needed and pipes straight into the next tool (redact or tx\-sign).
.IP \(bu 2
Only public data is stored in $W: addresses, UTXOs, the unsigned PSBT, the signed tx.
.IP \(bu 2
tx\-sign and tx\-broadcast each print the decoded transaction on /dev/tty and wait for a
typed code. Nothing is signed or sent without it.
.IP \(bu 2
Wallet passwords come from \-\-password\-file (first line), read by the tool, not by bash.
.IP \(bu 2
Bitcoin, except an Ethereum keystore or presale wallet, which sweeps ETH (\-\-rpc URL, \-\-chain\-id N).
.PP
Invoked by a POSIX shell instead of bash? dash < 0.5.11 (Ubuntu 22.04) has no pipefail and would exit 2,
so re\-exec under bash before the first bash\-only line.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
\-\-chain
\-\-chain\-id
\-\-count
\-\-fee\-rate
\-\-goal
\-\-password\-file
\-\-url
.fi
Each flag's meaning is in the SYNOPSIS usage line(s) above (taken from \-\-help).
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
.IP \(bu 2
Secrets never touch the disk or this script's variables: keys() re\-runs the reader
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status ok
.TP
3
no status field
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ echo "abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon about" > s; BIN="$BIN" bash "$R/recipes/recover.sh" s bc1qcr8te4kr609gcawutmrza0j4xv80jy8z306fyu \-\-goal addresses
# exit 0, last status: ok
$ echo hello world > f; BIN="$BIN" bash "$R/recipes/recover.sh" f bc1qcr8te4kr609gcawutmrza0j4xv80jy8z306fyu \-\-goal addresses
# exit 3, no status field
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: audit before use with real funds. See docs/SECURITY.md.
Run secret\-touching tools only inside ./blocktools run (sealed, offline).
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
